    "title": "Manchester City Defender Josko Gvardiol Signs New Contract",
    "text": "• Josko Gvardiol has signed a new five-year contract with Manchester City until 2031.\n• Gvardiol joined Manchester City in 2023 and had two years remaining on his deal at the Etihad Stadium.\n• Gvardiol was signed from Leipzig for 90 million euros ($99.2 million), making him one of the most expensive defenders in soccer history.\n• He has won five major trophies with Manchester City, including the Premier League title and FA Cup.\n• Gvardiol is 24 years old.\n• City director of football Hugo Viana said Josko is a player the club believes in and is committed to keeping their best talent.\n• Gvardiol believes Manchester City is the best club in the world to be at.",
    "summary": "The Croatia defender joined City in 2023 and had two years remaining on his deal at the Etihad Stadium. I truly believe we will have a lot of success in the coming years.” The 24-year-old Gvardiol joined City from Leipzig for 90 million euros ($99.2 million), ranking him among the most expensive defenders in soccer history. He has won five major trophies including the Premier League title and FA Cup during his time at the club. He is young, an outstanding professional and already one of the best defenders in the world,” City director of football Hugo Viana said.",
